{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Do not cut off the tribe of the families of the Kohathites.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, commanded Aaron and his sons to admonish the Levites, the sons of Kohath, and to guard them lest they come to excision (karet). And the Holy One, blessed be He, had compassion on the tribe of Levi, because he had surrendered himself for the sanctification of the Name at the [golden] calf, as it says (Exodus 32): ״והרגו איש את אחיו ואיש את רעהו ואיש את קרובו״ — and therefore He said, אל תכריתו — 'do not cut off.'" "<b>And by way of the Midrash.</b> אל תכריתו — thus did the Sages, of blessed memory, teach: all who are liable to excision (karet) and received lashes are exempt from their excision, as it says (Deuteronomy 25): ״והפילו השופט״ — it is written ״ארבעים יכנו״ — 'forty shall he strike him' — and it is written ״ונקלה אחיך״ — 'and your brother shall be degraded'; once he has been lashed, he is your brother. And why forty? Because man is formed in forty days, and transgressed the Torah that was given in forty days; the Torah says, let him be lashed forty and go free from his punishment. And so you find with the first man: when he was commanded and transgressed, the world was punished with forty punishments — the first man ten, and Eve ten, and the serpent ten, and the earth ten. Therefore when a man transgresses a commandment, he is lashed forty. So too you find in the wilderness, in the punishment of the spies: they were lashed forty years in the wilderness." "<b>The families of the Kohathites.</b> And it does not say 'the family of Kohath.' The Holy One, blessed be He, said: it is revealed and known before Me that Korah and his assembly are destined to contend against Moses and Aaron; even so, the Holy One, blessed be He, said: אל תכריתו — 'do not cut off.' He took half of His name and placed it upon Kohath, and said: הקהתי — 'the Kohathite' (My Kohathite). It is like a king who had a son who attached himself to robbers, and they were all caught. The king said: for the sake of my son I ransom them all now. And thus Scripture says (Isaiah 48): ״למען שמי אאריך אפי ותהלתי אחטם לך לבלתי הכריתך״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {2 "On the phrase 'half of His name': the letter ה in הקהתי is read as a divine suffix ('My Kohathite'), understood as bearing a letter of the divine name."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:30:16.534801892Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}